From 1fb8f501414bbf13e01fa54f5a3aabdc1f545be3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (DocuFast upgrade)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:12:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DPDP consent + customer deletion, audit log, status history,
 cron reconcile, RLS

Security / privacy (blueprint "Fix first" + Compliance):
- Consent checkbox and retention note on the upload step; no file can be
  chosen or uploaded until it is ticked. consent_at stored on the job.
- Customer-requested deletion: POST /api/jobs/[code]/delete, proven by a
  per-order secret token (kept in the customer's browser) or the full
  Razorpay payment id. Paid-but-unprinted orders are refused (shop must
  cancel/refund first). "Delete my file now" button on the status page.
- file_access_log table: every signed-link download by an agent is logged
  (replaces the console.log). Only signed, unexpired requests are logged.
- job_status_history table: every status change with actor and time;
  customer status page shows a safe history (status + time only).
- Owner audit endpoint GET /api/owner/audit?code= (history + file access).
- ensureSchema now enables row-level security (no policies) on every table.
  On Supabase the public schema is reachable through the REST API with the
  anon key; owner_auth (owner password hash) was found without RLS. The app
  connects as postgres, which bypasses RLS, so behaviour is unchanged.
- SECURITY.md updated to describe all of the above.

Poll path:
- Payment reconcile now also runs in the cleanup cron (before the abandoned
  sweep). pending.js skips reconcile + purge when LEAN_POLL=1. Default is
  unchanged because the cron is daily; see .env.example.

Tested: next build passes; 16 DB-logic checks and the new HTTP endpoints
exercised against a local Postgres; RLS flags verified on a fresh database.
